{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"docker.io/nodered/node-red","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:04:21.480Z","source":{"name":"Docker Hub","api":"https://hub.docker.com/v2/repositories/nodered/node-red/","page":"https://hub.docker.com/r/nodered/node-red"},"readme":"# ![logo](https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f6f37d429a9c6575007e1c72798e0de5.jpg?s=80&r=g&d=mm) Node-RED\n\n### Low-code programming for event-driven applications\n\nTo run Node-RED in Docker in its simplest form just run:\n```\ndocker run -it -p 1880:1880 -v myNodeREDdata:/data --name mynodered nodered/node-red\n```\nor for the minimal version\n```\ndocker run -it -p 1880:1880 -v myNodeREDdata:/data --name mynodered nodered/node-red:latest-minimal\n```\nThe minimal version does not contain build tools or support for projects.\n\n**Note**: RaspberryPI Zero and 1 users (Arm6 cpu) will need to use the specific tag name to install due to an upstream docker bug in the architecture detection.\nFor example :\n```\ndocker run -it -p 1880:1880 -v myNodeREDdata:/data --name mynodered nodered/node-red:1.0.1-10-minimal-arm32v6\n```\nfor the minimal node 10 version.\n\nFor more detailed information see our [docker](https://nodered.org/docs/getting-started/docker) guide.\n\nFor any questions please use the public [Node-RED discourse forum](https://discourse.nodered.org).\n\nFor general information about Node-RED please visit the [website](https://nodered.org).\n\nThis project is available on [github](https://github.com//node-red/node-red-docker).","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"nodered","url":"https://hub.docker.com/u/nodered","official":false,"verified":false},"registered":"2019-09-30T13:00:37.679021Z","updated":"2026-09-09T12:45:57.000432Z","categories":["Integration & delivery","API management","Internet of things"],"keywords":[],"license":null,"links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":324354906,"stars":770},"mediaTypes":["application/vnd.docker.container.image.v1+json","application/vnd.docker.distr